[{"sha":"69f26dbae7e1cd4532747cf0e85b60dcdd61e742","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDY5ZjI2ZGJhZTdlMWNkNDUzMjc0N2NmMGU4NWI2MGRjZGQ2MWU3NDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"StanleyYP Wang","email":"StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com","date":"2026-07-27T15:04:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-26T10:22:52Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix reg addr remap when addr is 0\n\nWhen addr is less than the hardcoded threshold in __mt7996_reg_addr,\nit indicates that remapping is unnecessary.\nCurrently, the flow remaps address 0x0 to MT_HIF_REMAP_BASE_L2,\nwhich is incorrect.\nTo address this, modify __mt7996_reg_addr to return INVALID_REG_ADDR\nif the address is not below the hardcoded value or is not present in\nthe mt7996_reg_map array.\nAdditionally, update the remap condition to check if addr is equal to\nINVALID_REG_ADDR.\n\nFixes: 3687854d3e7e (\"wifi: mt76: mt7996: add locking for accessing mapped registers\")\nSigned-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260727150434.1778520-5-nbd@nbd.name\nSigned-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>","tree":{"sha":"94715380272a45a080b36f0d32ed62d9d34ff66e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/94715380272a45a080b36f0d32ed62d9d34ff66e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/69f26dbae7e1cd4532747cf0e85b60dcdd61e742","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/69f26dbae7e1cd4532747cf0e85b60dcdd61e742","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/69f26dbae7e1cd4532747cf0e85b60dcdd61e742","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/69f26dbae7e1cd4532747cf0e85b60dcdd61e742/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f"}]},{"sha":"912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDkxMmM1MTk0NTA1OWYyNzMwNTRlMjQ4MDFiYmNmMDcyZWVjZWRiNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-07-27T15:04:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-26T10:22:27Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix MIB TX aggregation counter registers for mt7990\n\nThe MIB_TSCR0-7 counters read by mt7996_mac_update_stats() are\nhardcoded at the mt7996/mt7992 offsets 0x6b0-0x6d0, but mt7990 moved\nthem to 0x750-0x770, so TX AMPDU statistics were read from unrelated\nregisters on that chip. Move the offsets into the per-chip register\ntables.\n\nFixes: f6c87411d15f (\"wifi: mt76: mt7996: rework register mapping for mt7990\")\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260727150434.1778520-1-nbd@nbd.name\nSigned-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>","tree":{"sha":"5b7b000c605178571b493f589b6bcc63677ea49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/5b7b000c605178571b493f589b6bcc63677ea49c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/912c51945059f273054e24801bbcf072eecedb4f/comments","author":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b9533b83eb21ec8f8039f035eeca4339569864f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/b9533b83eb21ec8f8039f035eeca4339569864f0","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/b9533b83eb21ec8f8039f035eeca4339569864f0"}]},{"sha":"074472e615e94db31e23d0fef4a9ca9b085f5ce1","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDA3NDQ3MmU2MTVlOTRkYjMxZTIzZDBmZWY0YTljYTliMDg1ZjVjZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Howard Hsu","email":"howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com","date":"2026-07-27T15:04:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-25T09:55:25Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: mt7996: reject iTWT setup requests from MLD stations\n\nThe firmware does not support individual TWT agreements with non-AP MLDs,\nand the driver only tracks TWT flow state on the default link, which may\nnot be the link the agreement was negotiated on. Reject TWT setup\nrequests from MLD stations instead of programming an unsupported\nconfiguration.\n\nSigned-off-by: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260727150434.1778520-12-nbd@nbd.name\nSigned-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>","tree":{"sha":"57275a566bdc1f6440dfbae898ffdc66de0f01ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/57275a566bdc1f6440dfbae898ffdc66de0f01ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/074472e615e94db31e23d0fef4a9ca9b085f5ce1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/074472e615e94db31e23d0fef4a9ca9b085f5ce1","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/074472e615e94db31e23d0fef4a9ca9b085f5ce1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/074472e615e94db31e23d0fef4a9ca9b085f5ce1/comments","author":{"login":"haogroot","id":5622631,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjI2MzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5622631?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot","html_url":"https://github.com/haogroot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haogroot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756"}]},{"sha":"2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDJkNmQ2OWU3MTYyYWI4OGZhY2Y4ZjYxOGM0YjA3N2JkYzYzYWI3NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-07-27T15:04:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-25T09:55:25Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: mt7996: do not leave state behind after a failed WED attach\n\nmt7996_mmio_wed_init() set dev->mt76.hwrro_mode and rx_token_size while\nbuilding the WED configuration, before knowing whether the WED attach\ncan succeed. A failed attach left the enlarged rx_token_size behind and\nreset hwrro_mode to MT76_HWRRO_OFF, clobbering the values that another\nRX datapath owner may have configured earlier in probe: on Airoha\nplatforms with the wed_enable module parameter set, this broke the NPU\noffload configuration set up by mt76_npu_init() (NPU offload requires\nHW-RRO and a larger rx token space, and the attach always fails there\nsince no SoC has both an Airoha NPU and MTK WED).\n\nMove both assignments after a successful attach, next to the existing\nsuccess-only dma_dev/irq assignments. This is safe for the regular WED\nattach case: the first consumer of either field runs after probe\ncontinues (mtk_wed_device_attach() only invokes the init_buf callback;\nrx buffers are allocated via init_rx_buf from mtk_wed_start(), long\nafter mt7996_mmio_wed_init() has returned).\n\nWithin the WED configuration the HW-RRO checks were constant: the mode\nwas assigned unconditionally right before them, and the hif2 path is\nonly reachable after a successful main attach has set it. Resolve them\nto their constant values and drop the dead branches.\n\nFixes: 377aa17d2aed (\"wifi: mt76: mt7996: Add NPU offload support to MT7996 driver\")\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260727150434.1778520-7-nbd@nbd.name\nSigned-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>","tree":{"sha":"4241708b1b2eef06b6c94bc16d75d7248db98d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/4241708b1b2eef06b6c94bc16d75d7248db98d0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/2d6d69e7162ab88facf8f618c4b077bdc63ab756/comments","author":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9de658490af758f89c083605bd412310511fff17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/9de658490af758f89c083605bd412310511fff17","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/9de658490af758f89c083605bd412310511fff17"}]},{"sha":"c5a3bd91aa735b669618610d5f0ebfa5786845a6","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKGM1YTNiZDkxYWE3MzViNjY5NjE4NjEwZDVmMGViZmE1Nzg2ODQ1YTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mateus B. Cassiano","email":"mbc07@live.com","date":"2026-06-16T00:04:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-22T12:50:15Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: pass LED define via ccflags-y in driver submodules\n\nCommit d2b01fbc329b (\"mt76: pass LED define via ccflags-y\")\nconverted the top-level Makefile from the deprecated EXTRA_CFLAGS\nto ccflags-y so that -DCONFIG_MT76_LEDS keeps working now that\nkbuild no longer honours EXTRA_CFLAGS.\n\nHowever, ccflags-y (like EXTRA_CFLAGS before it) only applies to\nthe kbuild makefile it is set in and is not inherited by\nsubdirectories pulled in via obj-y/obj-m. The mt7603, mt7615 and\nmt7915 driver subdirectories each set their own\n\"EXTRA_CFLAGS += ... -DCONFIG_MT76_LEDS\", which is now a silent\nno-op. As a result CONFIG_MT76_LEDS is undefined when building\nmt7603/init.c, mt7615/init.c, mt7615/pci_init.c and mt7915/init.c,\nthe IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MT76_LEDS) blocks are compiled out, and the\nmt76-* LED class devices are never registered for these drivers.\n\nConvert these subdirectory Makefiles to ccflags-y as well.\n\nmt7996/Makefile never carried the define at all, even though\nmt7996/init.c has the same IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MT76_LEDS) checks for\nits LED callbacks and GPIO mux setup. Add ccflags-y there too so\nmt7996 LED support is enabled consistently with the other drivers.\n\nmt76x0, mt76x2, mt7921 and mt7925 contain no CONFIG_MT76_LEDS\nreferences and are left untouched.\n\nFixes: d2b01fbc329b (\"mt76: pass LED define via ccflags-y\")\nLink: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/1077\nSigned-off-by: Mateus B. Cassiano <mbc07@live.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bdcb3b6d60848cd1be1a6c511c59ab4e3b2592a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/4bdcb3b6d60848cd1be1a6c511c59ab4e3b2592a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/c5a3bd91aa735b669618610d5f0ebfa5786845a6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/c5a3bd91aa735b669618610d5f0ebfa5786845a6","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/c5a3bd91aa735b669618610d5f0ebfa5786845a6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/c5a3bd91aa735b669618610d5f0ebfa5786845a6/comments","author":{"login":"mbc07","id":8005966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMDU5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8005966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07","html_url":"https://github.com/mbc07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbc07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861"}]},{"sha":"254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDI1NGEzNDQyYjNhZDMyZmY3ZThjOTJkMWE4MjQ4MTUyNWM1YTM4NjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sriram R","email":"quic_srirrama@quicinc.com","date":"2026-02-19T19:42:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T13:44:01Z"},"message":"wifi: mac80211: fetch FILS discovery template by link ID\n\nCurrently, the FILS discovery template is always fetched from the default\nlink of a virtual interface in both Multi-Link Operation (MLO) and\nnon-MLO cases. However, in the MLO case there is a need to fetch the FILS\ndiscovery template from a specific link instead of the default link.\n\nHence, add support for fetching the FILS discovery template based on the\nlink ID from the corresponding link data.\n\nSigned-off-by: Sriram R <quic_srirrama@quicinc.com>\nCo-developed-by: Raj Kumar Bhagat <raj.bhagat@oss.qualcomm.com>\nSigned-off-by: Raj Kumar Bhagat <raj.bhagat@oss.qualcomm.com>\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260220-fils-prob-by-link-v1-1-a2746a853f75@oss.qualcomm.com\nSigned-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c5dc8458b43bbd2d7da7a13c50187c339dbc42f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/1c5dc8458b43bbd2d7da7a13c50187c339dbc42f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/254a3442b3ad32ff7e8c92d1a82481525c5a3861/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9abd11a8f8b2aee4c2f59c3aba157f35c51c797d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/9abd11a8f8b2aee4c2f59c3aba157f35c51c797d","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/9abd11a8f8b2aee4c2f59c3aba157f35c51c797d"}]},{"sha":"67c5f7ae2511d798097e5e202bda086f4ede2be0","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDY3YzVmN2FlMjUxMWQ3OTgwOTdlNWUyMDJiZGEwODZmNGVkZTJiZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sriram R","email":"quic_srirrama@quicinc.com","date":"2026-02-19T19:42:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T13:44:01Z"},"message":"wifi: mac80211: fetch unsolicited probe response template by link ID\n\nCurrently, the unsolicited probe response template is always fetched from\nthe default link of a virtual interface in both Multi-Link Operation (MLO)\nand non-MLO cases. However, in the MLO case there is a need to fetch the\nunsolicited probe response template from a specific link instead of the\ndefault link.\n\nHence, add support for fetching the unsolicited probe response template\nbased on the link ID from the corresponding link data.\n\nSigned-off-by: Sriram R <quic_srirrama@quicinc.com>\nCo-developed-by: Raj Kumar Bhagat <raj.bhagat@oss.qualcomm.com>\nSigned-off-by: Raj Kumar Bhagat <raj.bhagat@oss.qualcomm.com>\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260220-fils-prob-by-link-v1-2-a2746a853f75@oss.qualcomm.com\nSigned-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>","tree":{"sha":"422d1aadc86a8ce55cf31dc7b7ffd5382690dbf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/422d1aadc86a8ce55cf31dc7b7ffd5382690dbf2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/67c5f7ae2511d798097e5e202bda086f4ede2be0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/67c5f7ae2511d798097e5e202bda086f4ede2be0","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/67c5f7ae2511d798097e5e202bda086f4ede2be0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/67c5f7ae2511d798097e5e202bda086f4ede2be0/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d"}]},{"sha":"d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKGQ0OTcyMWMyMDVjNDU3YmNmZjMwYWQ4NjA5NjYzZTljOTY1ZmYwNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes Berg","email":"johannes.berg@intel.com","date":"2026-02-26T17:36:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T13:44:01Z"},"message":"wifi: move action code from per-type frame structs\n\nThe action code actually serves to identify the type of action\nframe, so it really isn't part of the per-type structure. Pull\nit out and have it in the general action frame format.\n\nIn theory, whether or not the action code is present in this\nway is up to each category, but all categories that are defined\nright now all have that value.\n\nWhile at it, and since this change requires changing all users,\nremove the 'u' and make it an anonymous union in this case, so\nthat all code using this changes.\n\nChange IEEE80211_MIN_ACTION_SIZE to take an argument which says\nhow much of the frame is needed, e.g. category, action_code or\nthe specific frame type that's defined in the union. Again this\nalso ensures that all code is updated.\n\nIn some cases, fix bugs where the SKB length was checked after\nhaving accessed beyond the checked length, in particular in FTM\ncode, e.g. ieee80211_is_ftm().\n\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260226183607.67e71846b59e.I9a24328e3ffcaae179466a935f1c3345029f9961@changeid\nSigned-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>","tree":{"sha":"114d604a34e91075e48c14f66647ec8996681487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/114d604a34e91075e48c14f66647ec8996681487"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/d49721c205c457bcff30ad8609663e9c965ff05d/comments","author":{"login":"jmberg-intel","id":96500427,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcB6yw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96500427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel","html_url":"https://github.com/jmberg-intel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmberg-intel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c84469c8fc854775fab02ec1e0b20df137c41b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/2c84469c8fc854775fab02ec1e0b20df137c41b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/2c84469c8fc854775fab02ec1e0b20df137c41b6"}]},{"sha":"95cb6eefae12b97bb28331cc3d63ff459e49c4a1","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKDk1Y2I2ZWVmYWUxMmI5N2JiMjgzMzFjYzNkNjNmZjQ1OWU0OWM0YTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T12:58:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T13:42:32Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: mt7996: take over connection monitoring\n\nmt76 runs its own beacon monitor. mt76_beacon_mon_check() counts a miss\nfor each affiliated link of an MLD, and it stops the count while the phy\nis off channel. mt7996 supplies it through mt76_rx_beacon(), but it does\nnot set CONNECTION_MONITOR. Therefore mac80211 also starts its legacy\nmonitor.\n\nThe legacy monitor knows one interface, not a set of links. It also\ncounts while the radio serves a different link. After seven beacon\nintervals it removes an association that still carries traffic on the\nother links.\n\nSet the CONNECTION_MONITOR flag to disable the legacy monitor.\n\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260818125825.395538-3-nbd@nbd.name\nSigned-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>","tree":{"sha":"0ccf69394f72d35f62fdfcb511430492d4fcfed9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/0ccf69394f72d35f62fdfcb511430492d4fcfed9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/95cb6eefae12b97bb28331cc3d63ff459e49c4a1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/95cb6eefae12b97bb28331cc3d63ff459e49c4a1","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/95cb6eefae12b97bb28331cc3d63ff459e49c4a1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/95cb6eefae12b97bb28331cc3d63ff459e49c4a1/comments","author":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nbd168","id":2529314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2529314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168","html_url":"https://github.com/nbd168","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nbd168/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"26e36bf38f1560c3243151138dee2efe2c80014e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/26e36bf38f1560c3243151138dee2efe2c80014e","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/26e36bf38f1560c3243151138dee2efe2c80014e"}]},{"sha":"dec412a05ac40688a46ab871036b4fb87a7b8910","node_id":"C_kwDOAZrr3NoAKGRlYzQxMmEwNWFjNDA2ODhhNDZhYjg3MTAzNmI0ZmI4N2E3Yjg5MTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T12:58:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"Felix Fietkau","email":"nbd@nbd.name","date":"2026-08-18T13:42:32Z"},"message":"wifi: mt76: mt7996: program a link again if the driver holds it\n\nThe firmware needs the driver to remove active links from the BSSINFO table\nwhen it destroys the interface. A link therefore stays registered from its\nfirst chanctx assignment until the interface goes away. If the driver holds\nthe link already, a second add does nothing.\n\nmac80211 gives a non-AP MLD a new address each time it sets a link up. A link\nthat comes back after a failed attempt thus carries an address that the\nhardware does not know, on a BSS that the driver never programs again. The\nstation then authenticates from an address that nothing answers. The failure\nrepeats until the driver tears the interface down for good.\n\nProgram the address and the BSS again. This is the pair that the initial add\nsets up. For a station it does what mt7996_mcu_mld_link_oper() does for an AP.\n\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20260818125825.395538-1-nbd@nbd.name\nSigned-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>","tree":{"sha":"5c7fe2ce06c63ac3ecadd68e82205a4f8cabb9f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/trees/5c7fe2ce06c63ac3ecadd68e82205a4f8cabb9f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/git/commits/dec412a05ac40688a46ab871036b4fb87a7b8910","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/dec412a05ac40688a46ab871036b4fb87a7b8910","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/dec412a05ac40688a46ab871036b4fb87a7b8910","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/mt76/commits/dec412a05ac40688a46ab871036b4fb87a7b8910/comments","author":{"login":"nbd168","id":